445 0 obj
<<
/A 2135 0 R
/ADBE_FT 2136 0 R
/C /adbe_style_004000
/ID (AD260921-1009-1222-ADBE-000000003825)
/K 0
/P 42 0 R
/Pg 13 0 R
/S /Figure
/Alt (Data pillars for Trait Causal Models. Each pillar provides complementary causal or correlative information on connections between biological layers. The first pillar represents genome-wide association studies with causal links of variants and genes to traits, showing biased discoveries due to selection and limited power for trans-QTLs. The second pillar represents perturb-seq studies showing cis- and trans-effects of genetic perturbations, with confounded direct and indirect effects and limited set of accessible cell types. The third pillar represents observational omics studies showing molecular phenotypes across cell types and tissue changes associated with clinical phenotypes, distinguishing cause from consequence.)
/Contents (Data pillars for Trait Causal Models. Each pillar provides complementary causal or correlative information on connections between biological layers. The first pillar represents genome-wide association studies with causal links of variants and genes to traits, showing biased discoveries due to selection and limited power for trans-QTLs. The second pillar represents perturb-seq studies showing cis- and trans-effects of genetic perturbations, with confounded direct and indirect effects and limited set of accessible cell types. The third pillar represents observational omics studies showing molecular phenotypes across cell types and tissue changes associated with clinical phenotypes, distinguishing cause from consequence.)
>>
endobj
